              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઘૂમવું — ghūmvũ — \"to whirl round\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "રાત્રે લોકો મંડપમાં ગરબે ઘૂમ્યા. rātre loko manḍapmā̃ garbe ghūmyā. At night people whirled round in the garba in the pavilion."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he …): તે ગરબે ઘૂમ્યો, te garbe ghūmyo."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઘૂમવું (ghūmvũ) comes from ghummati, a form CDIAL reconstructs, where it lists Gujarati ghumvũ, glossed \"to revolve in the mind\" (CDIAL 4485). In the dance it is moving round and round: ગરબે ઘૂમ્યા, they danced the garba."
            }
          ]
